---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "June 18, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — AllByte Studios">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-body">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        These terms govern your use of <strong>allbyte.studio</strong> and
        <em>The Chronicles of Nesis</em>, operated by AllByte Studios, a solo
        independent game developer (&ldquo;I,&rdquo; &ldquo;me,&rdquo; or
        &ldquo;AllByte&rdquo;). By using the site, you agree to these terms. If
        you don't agree, please don't use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        The site provides a browser-playable build of <em>The Chronicles of
        Nesis</em>, a development blog, artwork and music showcases, and
        membership features. I may add, change, or remove features at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        Accounts and sign-in are handled through Patreon. You are responsible for
        activity under your account and for keeping your Patreon credentials
        secure. You must provide accurate information and be old enough to use
        Patreon in your jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>Memberships and payments</h2>
      <p>
        Membership tiers are offered and billed entirely through Patreon and are
        subject to <a href="https://policies.patreon.com/" rel="noopener">Patreon's
        terms</a>. Tiers unlock access to certain site and game content. You can
        change or cancel your membership at any time through Patreon; I do not
        process payments and cannot issue charges or refunds directly &mdash;
        billing matters are handled by Patreon.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        All artwork, music, fonts, characters, story, game content, and code on
        this site are created and owned by AllByte Studios (or used under
        license) and are protected by copyright. The art, music, and typography
        are entirely handcrafted. You may not copy, redistribute, extract,
        decompile, or repackage any of these assets, in whole or in part, without
        my written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Game license</h2>
      <p>
        I grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to play
        <em>The Chronicles of Nesis</em> through this site for your own personal,
        non-commercial enjoyment. You may not host, mirror, resell, or
        commercially exploit the game or its assets.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Attempt to circumvent membership gates or access controls.</li>
        <li>Extract, scrape, or reverse-engineer game assets or source.</li>
        <li>Disrupt, overload, or attempt to gain unauthorized access to the site or its backend.</li>
        <li>Use the site to break any applicable law or to infringe others' rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        The site and game are provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as
        available,&rdquo; without warranties of any kind. As a solo developer, I
        can't guarantee the site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that saves
        will never be lost &mdash; though I do my best to keep everything working.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, AllByte Studios will not be liable
        for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your
        use of the site or game.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        I may update these terms as the site evolves. Continued use after an
        update means you accept the revised terms. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo;
        date above reflects the current version.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the state
        in which AllByte Studios operates, without regard to conflict-of-law
        rules.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email
        <a href="mailto:allbytestudios@gmail.com">allbytestudios@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer theme="engine" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    background: #1a1e26;
    color: #e0e7ff;
    min-height: 80dvh;
    padding: 3rem 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .legal-body {
    max-width: 46rem;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: "Courier New", Courier, monospace;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: "AllByteCustom", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    color: #a7f3d0;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: "AllByteCustom", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: #a7f3d0;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .updated {
    color: rgba(224, 231, 255, 0.5);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: rgba(224, 231, 255, 0.82);
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li {
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
  }

  a {
    color: #a7f3d0;
  }

  strong {
    color: #e0e7ff;
  }
</style>
